  "_why": "FROZEN structural W-7, captured 2026-09-11 from the last GIT-TRACKED copy (commit fcd7963a7~1), NOT the currently published one -- deliberately.\nThis pins that the completion denominator EXCLUDES fields the user cannot act on. It needs BOTH shapes to be non-empty: statically hidden fields, and show_if chains where filling one field reveals another.\nThe PUBLISHED W-7 no longer has any hidden field: the maintainer removed the acceptance-agent block (agent_phone, agent_fax, agent_ein, agent_ptin, agent_name_and_title, agent_company_name, agent_office_code) in the schema editor, and those were the 7. So this test's premise died when the FORM was fixed, not when the kit left git -- it would have broken on the next refresh either way. Freezing the older copy keeps the RULE under test while the form moves on, which is the whole point of a frozen specimen.\nSTRUCTURE ONLY: labels, help text and pdf geometry stripped -- counting never reads them. Do not hand-edit.",
